# Build output
build/bin/
frontend/dist/

# Throwaway experiments, probe tests, review screenshots and stray logs. Anything
# that is not project source goes here instead of the repository root.
scratch/

# Runtime config of the QQ protocol backend (credentials and access tokens),
# written to the working directory when the backend is started from the repo
# root. PetPC's own config.json lives in its data directory, not here.
/config.json

# A second copy of the sandboxed toolchain (.dev/, Go module cache, npm cache,
# test binaries) nested under the repository. Same reasoning as .dev/* below.
/pet_pc/

# ACL backup/restore reports left by workspace permission repair tooling.
/.acl-recovery/
/.dsh-file-attachment/

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Frontend dependencies
node_modules/

# Local development toolchain and scratch space created by this workspace's
# sandboxed setup (Go module cache, Wails CLI, test data, screenshots).
#
# The whole directory is excluded, then the three frontend verification gates are
# put back: README documents them as the project's regression checks (structure,
# real-browser behaviour, geometry dump), so they are project source rather than
# scratch, and a change to a gate has to be reviewable alongside the code it
# guards. Everything else under .dev/ (hundreds of MB of toolchain and probe
# output) stays out.
.dev/*
!.dev/check-frontend.cjs
!.dev/run-frontend-harness.cjs
!.dev/layout-report.cjs

# Wails generated native bindings are committed on purpose so the frontend
# type-checks without running the CLI; nothing to ignore for them here.

# Python bytecode left by the archived probe scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent session memory (tool scratch, not project source).
.memsearch/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# The plugin market lives in market/ as its own git repository (see
# openspec/changes/plugin-market). Ignoring it here keeps the host repo from
# tracking it as an embedded repository.
market/

# The plugin-surface pixel gate is the fourth frontend verification gate, and it
# is project source for the same reason the other three are.
!.dev/verify-plugin-surface.ps1

# The plugin market's real-window gate is the fifth, and it was the one gate
# missing from this list: it is named by .dev/check-all.ps1 and it verifies the
# market window's frame, size, address row and detail-pane edge, but with no
# whitelist entry here it was ignored by git - so the change that introduced it
# could not actually land it, and a later fix to the gate would not have been
# reviewable next to the code it guards. Same reasoning as the four above.
!.dev/verify-plugin-market.ps1

# The ENTRY POINT of every gate, and the two scripts it cannot run without.
#
# This is the same defect as the two notes above, one level up: check-all.ps1 is
# the one command README documents for "run every gate", it dot-sources env.ps1
# for the toolchain and launches verify-region.ps1 / verify-live.ps1 as child
# processes - and NONE of those four were whitelisted, so the only documented way
# to reproduce a green build was the one file git would not accept. A gate that
# cannot be committed is a gate that dies with the machine that wrote it.
#
# The whitelist is now closed over the dependency: everything .dev/check-all.ps1
# reaches by path is tracked. Everything else under .dev/ (~200 probe scripts,
# screenshots, CSV dumps, toolchain archives) stays ignored.
!.dev/check-all.ps1
!.dev/env.ps1
!.dev/verify-region.ps1
!.dev/verify-live.ps1

# The plugin market is a third Wails program, so its bundle is build output for
# the same reason frontend/dist/ is. The rest of the program (Go sources, the
# wailsjs bindings, index.html) is source and stays tracked.
tools/plugin-market/frontend/dist/
tools/plugin-market/build/bin/
tools/plugin-market/*.exe
